----- SOURCE CODE

pub type Wibble {
    Wibble(field1: Int, field2: Int)
}

pub fn main() {
  let wibble = Wibble(1, 2)
  let wobble = Wibble(field1: 0, ..wibble)
}
        

----- ERROR
error: Syntax error
  ┌─ /src/parse/error.gleam:8:34
  │
8 │   let wobble = Wibble(field1: 0, ..wibble)
  │                                  ^^^^^^^^ I wasn't expecting a record update here

When updating a record, the previous record comes before the fields to change

    let record = Record(field1:, field2:)
    let updated_record = Record(..record, field1: "new_value")

See: https://tour.gleam.run/data-types/record-updates/
